# Feedback System architecture

## Reference only
- `Courier-Dashboard/` and `Personal Notedbook/` are **reference** (gitignored). Copy patterns; do not import their code into the product app.
- Prefer Courier patterns: thin pages → `lib/` for data access → API routes for privileged writes → Postgres RPC for heavy/admin reads later.

## Customer form → Supabase
- Public customer form lives at `/` (multi-step). On **Submit**, POST `/api/feedback`.
- API validates with `lib/feedbackValidation.ts`, then inserts via `getSupabaseAdmin()` into `feedback_entries`.
- Do **not** expose service role to the browser. Do not insert from the client for production submissions.
- Schema source of truth: `database/schema.sql`.

## Admin panel (`/admin`)
- Login via **Supabase Auth** (`signInWithPassword`) — only users in Supabase Authentication can sign in.
- After Auth succeeds, set app session cookie `feedback_admin_session` (signed with `JWT_SECRET`) carrying `userId`, `email`, `name`.
- Middleware guards `/admin/*` except `/admin/login`.
- List/detail via `/api/admin/feedback` with service role; never expose admin APIs without session check.
- Brand name / question labels: configure later from admin settings (do not hardcode client brands).

## Layering
- `app/` — routes & UI pages only
- `components/` — UI
- `lib/` — options, validation, supabase clients
- `database/` — SQL schema / future RPCs (`rpc_*`)
- Admin panel (later): separate route group; list/filter via RPC + page size caps, never pull all rows client-side for reports

## Demo Mode & portfolio (when built)
- Follow Personal Notedbook `Portfolio-Project-Setup-Prompt.md`: Phase 1 `demo-mode/` offline clone → Documentation → screenshots → rules → README.
- Never fold `demo-mode/` into the root production build (`tsconfig` / eslint / vercel exclude).
- Docs screenshots only under `Documentation/images/`; professional English; no real PII in seeds; no passwords in `demo.json`.

## Product tone
- Client-facing copy: clear professional English.
- Fictional seed data only in demos.
